.TH VECMAP 1 "October 2026" "vecmap 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vecmap \- vector database attack\-surface assessment framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vecmap
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ...]
.br
.B vecmap
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B vecmap
.BR \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vecmap
is a locally\-run, sqlmap\-style attack\-surface assessment framework for vector
databases anywhere on the network (internet, intranet, or production). It fingerprints the target product and
version, probes read\-only management endpoints, correlates the identified
version against embedded GitHub Security Advisory snapshots (CVE/CNVD), and,
in deep mode, enumerates collections and extracts records and vector samples.
.P
All probes are strictly read\-only (GET/HEAD/OPTIONS and read\-only POST).
Destructive endpoints such as
.B /management/stop
are hard\-denied and never invoked. Evidence, sessions, collections, records
and findings are persisted in a local SQLite database with WAL.
.P
Supported vendors: Qdrant, Milvus, Weaviate, Chroma, Redis/RediSearch,
Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, PostgreSQL pgvector, Typesense, Pinecone, Vespa.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Attack\-surface scan: fingerprinting, read\-only probes, advisory correlation,
risk findings. Use
.B \-\-mode deep
or
.B \-\-extract
to enumerate collections and extract records.
.TP
.B discover
Concurrent TCP/HTTP/TLS/gRPC/RESP port discovery across hosts or CIDR ranges.
.TP
.B dump
Deep enumeration and record extraction (implies
.BR "\-\-mode deep \-\-extract" ).
.TP
.B sessions
List locally persisted sessions, newest first.
.TP
.B report
Render a session report (markdown, json or html) offline.
.TP
.B advisories
List the built\-in advisory catalog (embedded GHSA snapshots).
.TP
.B delete
Delete a session and all associated evidence (cascading).
.TP
.B version
Print the version string.
.TP
.B help
Show the overview or per\-command usage.
.TP
.B man
Print this manual page in roff format.
.TP
.B completion
Print a bash or zsh completion script.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Local database path. Default:
.BR ~/.vecmap/vecmap.db
(overridden by the
.B VECMAP_DB
environment variable).
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " en|zh"
UI and report language. Default from
.BR VECMAP_LANG ,
otherwise en.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Verbose protocol logging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help for the command.
.SH SCAN AND DUMP OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Session name.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " standard|deep"
Scan mode; deep enumerates and extracts (default standard).
.TP
.BI \-\-ports " PORTS"
Ports for bare hosts (comma list).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DUR"
Per\-request timeout (default 8s).
.TP
.BI \-\-concurrency " N"
Concurrency (default 8).
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " N"
Request rate limit in requests per second.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.B \-\-fuzz
Extended read\-only path probing.
.TP
.B \-\-extract
Extract records (implies deep mode).
.TP
.BI \-\-collection " NAME"
Restrict enumeration to a single collection.
.TP
.BI \-\-namespace " NS"
Restrict enumeration to a single namespace.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-records " N"
Record extraction limit (default 200).
.TP
.BI \-\-batch " N"
Pagination size (default 100).
.TP
.B \-\-vectors
Include vector samples in extraction.
.TP
.BI \-\-user\-agent " UA"
Custom User\-Agent.
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " URL"
HTTP(S) proxy.
.TP
.BI \-\-header " K:V"
Extra request header (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-advisories " PATH"
Import an external advisories JSON file (unverified entries are listed only).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Do not persist anything.
.SH AUTHENTICATION OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-key " KEY"
API key; the header is chosen per vendor (Qdrant
.IR api\-key ,
Typesense
.IR X\-TYPESENSE\-API\-KEY ,
Pinecone
.IR Api\-Key ,
Elasticsearch/OpenSearch
.IR ApiKey ,
others
.IR Bearer ).
.TP
.BI \-\-bearer " TOKEN"
Authorization: Bearer token.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " USER"
Basic\-auth username.
.TP
.BI \-\-pass " PASS"
Basic\-auth password.
.TP
.BI \-\-database " NAME"
Database name, tenant path, or Redis DB number.
.TP
.BI \-\-dsn " DSN"
PostgreSQL connection string.
.SH SCOPE AND AUTHORIZATION OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-scope\-cidr " CIDR"
Authorized CIDR (repeatable). When set, unmatched hosts are denied.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope\-domain " DOMAIN"
Authorized domain (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-scope\-port " PORT"
Authorized port (repeatable or comma list).
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-cidr " CIDR"
Excluded CIDR (repeatable). Exclusion\-only scopes are otherwise permissive.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-domain " DOMAIN"
Excluded domain (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-authorize
Confirmation that written authorization has been obtained (required).
.SH TARGET FORMATS
URLs
.RI ( http://host:6333 ", " https://host ", " redis://host:6379 ", "
.BR postgres://user:pass@host/db ", " grpc://host:19530 ),
host:port pairs
.RI ( 10.0.0.5:6333 ),
and CIDR ranges
.RI ( 10.0.0.0/24 ,
expanded across
.BR \-\-ports ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
# Public production target (any internet host, like sqlmap)
vecmap scan \-\-authorize \-\-api\-key KEY https://vecdb.prod.example.com:6333
# Intranet asset within an authorized CIDR
vecmap scan \-\-authorize \-\-scope\-cidr 10.0.0.0/24 http://10.0.0.5:6333
vecmap dump \-\-authorize \-\-max\-records 500 \-\-vectors http://10.0.0.5:6333
vecmap discover \-\-authorize \-\-scope\-cidr 10.0.0.0/24 10.0.0.0/24
vecmap report \-\-session ses_1234abcd \-\-format html \-\-output report.html
vecmap advisories
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (network, database, adapter failure).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown command, missing required argument, missing
.BR \-\-authorize ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VECMAP_DB
Default database path (overrides
.BR ~/.vecmap/vecmap.db ).
.TP
.B VECMAP_LANG
Default UI language (en|zh).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output when set (standard convention).
.TP
.B HTTP_PROXY ", " HTTPS_PROXY
Honored by the HTTP client when
.B \-\-proxy
is not set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.vecmap/vecmap.db
Local session database (directory 0700, file 0600, WAL enabled).
.TP
.I <\-\-output path>
Session reports, written with 0600 permissions.
.SH SECURITY AND AUTHORIZATION
You must obtain written permission for every target before scanning and pass
.BR \-\-authorize .
Unauthorized scanning of systems you do not own or operate is illegal in most
jurisdictions. vecmap performs no exploits, no destructive operations, and no
denial\-of\-service; it is a reconnaissance and extraction tool only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vecmap\-help (1),
the MITRE ATT&CK framework,
the GitHub Advisory Database
.RI ( https://github.com/advisories ).
.SH AUTHOR
vecmap project contributors.
